& [Intent]
  + close the caller bootstrap gap by discovering bounded handle candidates without exposing full state

& [Work]
  + preserved source and completed SJS review and phase lock before implementation
  + implemented bootstrap and root-pinned selector forms with six intersecting constraints
  + preserved deterministic digest order bounded result count and explicit truncation
  + committed exact handles and entry digests under selector and response digests
  + exposed a bounded strict JSON stdin-to-stdout discovery command
  + tested filtering zero matches mutations command boundaries workspace regression and strict lint

& [Observation]
  + a caller can now bootstrap from no registry knowledge receive a root and bounded handles then pin all subsequent discovery or custody queries
  + this is the first practical catalogue layer but intentionally remains structural rather than semantic
  + semantic SOP term-to-handle association should be its own next data model rather than overloading checkpoint identity

& [FacultyAttribution]
  + Honesty separates bootstrap snapshot identity from provenance and semantic search
  + Security validates roots bounds prefixes order handles digests and body denials
  + Planner composes exact filter intersections and bounded output
  + Weaver joins discovery to custody without embedding custody
  + Scribe preserves selector response and entry identities
  + Refiner bounds output and keeps state bodies out
  + Observer compares every result with direct registry filtering

& [Next]
